  "provenance": {
    "physical_parameters": {
      "origin": "inferred",
      "note": "Golf 1.6 TDI / EA288-inspired warm common-rail I4. Pole Position Production identifies its 2019 Golf Variant recording as a 1.6 litre four-cylinder turbo diesel: https://pole.se/product/golf-variant-tdi-2019/ . VW Self-study Programme 891143C, The Golf 2014, printed p.20 supplies earlier CLHA-family bore 79.5 mm, stroke 80.5 mm, compression 16.2:1, and four valves: https://www.vaglinks.com/Docs/SSP/VWUSA.COM_SSP_891143C_2014_Golf.pdf . These family dimensions do not identify the exact recorded engine code or ECU calibration. Two 2 mg pilots at -18/-9 degrees and 38 mg main at -1 degree ATDC are authored, all scaled by fueling. Injector needle/rail pressure and ECU schedules are not solved. Rod length, cam windows/areas, gas temperatures, heat transfer, ignition coefficients and steady intake/exhaust boundary map are authored. Load-dependent boost up to 211325 Pa absolute at 2200-2700 RPM represents prescribed reservoirs, not compressor/turbine dynamics or turbo lag; oxygen fraction is fixed and EGR is not solved. No measured power/torque/emissions claim. The 4500 RPM bake row holds the authored 3800 RPM reservoir states; no additional boost or measured high-speed calibration is inferred. Inline-inertia reciprocating mass of .45 kg per cylinder is an authored effective mass, not a measured Golf piston/rod mass."
    },
    "presentation": {
      "origin": "artistic",
      "note": "Separate engine-microphone ramp candidate, based on the idle-reference candidate. Selected reference: https://soundcloud.com/polepositionproduction/vw-golf-diesel-t5-onbrd-1 , Pole Position Production T5 onboard engine mix, public WAV SHA256 04580414c33e50e724594ddad0110e584aa71b01c70677da9012043cf8110428. Harmonic ladder suggests about 1300 to 4470 RPM and back; throttle/fuel state is not logged. Exterior T7 remains the separate idle reference. No recording PCM or measured impulse response is embedded. Version 14 adds primary/secondary kinematic inertia for parallel cylinder axes from native crank radius, connecting rod length, firing phases and an authored .45 kg reciprocating mass per cylinder. Force scales with angular speed squared and continues at fuel cut. Authored 110 Hz Q2.5 radiation, 140 Hz highpass and 500 Hz lowpass, .0004 PCM/N gain. This is a physically motivated acoustic component, not a unique identification of the recorded sound, solved mounts/balance shafts or crank-speed dynamics. Preserve original gas sources in the existing 70 cells, add a 4500 RPM row using the last authored reservoirs. Increase block modes at/above 550 Hz by 1.7; coast mechanical gain 2 and movement 1, flow texture gain1.2 HP200 LP1000 to preserve mechanical/flow detail on rundown. Prior engine.json and idle-reference-candidate.json are unchanged. Listening approval pending; see RAMP_REFERENCE.md. Metallic-rattle audition: lower valve base resonance from 1650 to 1250 Hz, raise valve gain .02 to .025, reduce smooth contact duration .8 to .45 ms and increase ring decay 3.5 to 4 ms. Refocus the former 1050 Hz block mode at 1280 Hz Q7 gain2.4e-6, 1700 Hz Q4.5 gain1.2e-6, 2550 Hz Q3.5 gain6.9e-7; reduce 4600 Hz gain to 65 percent. These are authored acoustic choices following user feedback that the engine-mic ramp candidate lacked metallic rattle, not identified part resonances. Retain low block modes, inertia, pressure envelope, all exhaust/intake/coast controls, seeds and native gas sources. Prior engine-ramp-candidate.json unchanged. See RATTLE_REFERENCE.md; listening approval pending."
